adr: 0227
file: selfhost/compiler.pas
kills: constexpr_errors
why: D.10 makes sqrt of a negative value an error, and the emitted code traps on it. The fold is performed by this compiler's own arithmetic, so a guard that lets the call happen aborts the compiler on the very program it exists to diagnose. That is the difference between folding an error and committing one, and it is why every guard here is asked before the operation rather than after.
--- old
              if x < 0.0 then begin
                ErrorAt(e^.line, e^.col);
                writeln('sqrt of a negative value in a constant expression');
--- new
              if false then begin
                ErrorAt(e^.line, e^.col);
                writeln('sqrt of a negative value in a constant expression');
